     "- [ ] `build/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/execute-typed-graph-under-declared-build-effects` Execute typed graph under declared build effects\n\nStatus: Open\n\nEvidence baseline: [Build architecture](../../docs/phase-12-build-package-and-artifact-system/166-pkg2-build-system-architecture.md)\n\nClosing evidence: Clean build node receipts and undeclared environment/network/shell rejection. SAFE14 also denies undeclared postinstall, model/tool, compiler IR and unproven native generation/registry authority; permitted effects carry provider, scope, grant and trace, and hermetic release effects are replayable or have pinned outputs. Negative fixtures prove denial occurs before the external effect. Criterion `integration/build-input-capture`: Capture all declared external, session, configuration and script inputs affecting build outputs in reproducibility artifacts, or reject/mark nonhermetic behavior according to build policy. Accepted fixture: Capture declared external/session/configuration/script/environment/network/file inputs affecting build outputs with source and generator provenance. Negative fixture: Reject unrecorded nonhermetic influence or explicitly mark it according to the declared reproducibility policy; never silently certify hermeticity. Required evidence: build-input manifest and clean/replayed input-drift fixture; bind source/compiler/profile/target/provider identities, source-mapped stable diagnostics and every applicable source facet field/exception/negative condition listed for this criterion in specs/requirement-reconciliation/domain-gap-completion.edn. Dependencies consume auth/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/enforce-grant-intersection-attenuation-revocation-phase-and-lifetime, schema outputs under their stated contracts; no whole-component completion prerequisite. Status: Open; implementation acceptance unassessed."},
