     "- [ ] `legality/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/complete-safe-code-classification-and-taintunsafe-boundaries` Complete safe-code classification and taint/unsafe boundaries\n\nStatus: Open\n\nEvidence baseline: [Safety contract](../../bootstrap/clojure/src/gravity/c10_safety_analysis/contract.clj)\n\nClosing evidence: Every dangerous operation classified and unclassified operations rejected. Under the [SAFE1/SAFE6-SAFE11/SAFE15 contracts](plan.md), inspect real checks before operations with defined profile-legal failure, complete unsafe audits even when permitted, wrapper preconditions and cleanup, source-bound review invalidation and dependency policy. Reject incomplete FFI contracts, unsupported atomics, implicit narrowing, undeclared relaxed numerics, taint loss, incompatible sanitizers and unvalidated deserialization; preserve residual taint and secret redaction. Emit inspectable outcome, proof, trust and audit records; internal-only unsafe boundaries confer no safe public API. Explicit wrapping/saturating conversions retain their unresolved relation to checked/proven narrowing. Runtime/provider execution and domain-specific consumers require their own evidence. P12: proof consumers check theorem/source/certificate/hash-chain/trusted-kernel/assumption/profile/target agreement; unverified imports are ignored or rejected only as policy states. Proof production and symbolic lowering are separate Math producer interfaces; a profile check alone cannot close them. Foundation requirement gravity/safety-family-conformance: Exercise each claimed safety family on accepted safe programs, rejected illegal programs and explicit audited unsafe-island cases; retain the applicable proven-safe, runtime-checked, rejected or unsafe-island outcome, owning diagnostics and evidence. Refusals: Reject an unclassified dangerous operation, hidden unsafe path, stale proof/audit or missing actual runtime-check failure case; no fifth implicit outcome or undefined safe behavior is allowed. Evidence: retain the exact source/compiler/profile/target and applicable provider/checker identities, actual positive products and negative diagnostics for this criterion. Consume these actual dependency artifacts (not whole-component completion): runtime/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/implement-explicit-family-selection-and-no-runtime-rejection - Selected runtime/provider service contracts and actual link/load/service-use evidence; pass-evidence - Actual subject-bound checker/proof/certificate/audit/replay/test evidence and verdicts. Foundation requirement gravity/unsafe-island-safe-api-eligibility: Expose unsafe-backed functionality as a safe API only when the wrapper proves or checks every required precondition and cleanup obligation, with source-bound audit and actual boundary tests; preserve internal-only status as a separate permitted boundary. Refusals: Reject invalid state escaping into safe code, a missing wrapper test/audit, an unproved precondition or treating internal-only unsafe code as a safe exported API. Evidence: retain the exact source/compiler/profile/target and applicable provider/checker identities, actual positive products and negative diagnostics for this criterion. Consume these actual dependency artifacts (not whole-component completion): runtime/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/implement-explicit-family-selection-and-no-runtime-rejection - Selected runtime/provider service contracts and actual link/load/service-use evidence; legality/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/complete-profile-restrictions-and-generated-form-checks - Expanded source profile/effect/grant facts and checked/delegated/rejected legality products."},
