     "- [ ] `legality/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/preserve-obligations-into-mir-and-runtime-execution` Preserve obligations into MIR and runtime execution\n\nStatus: Open\n\nEvidence baseline: [Safety pipeline](../../bootstrap/clojure/src/gravity/c10_safety_analysis/pipeline.clj)\n\nClosing evidence: Surviving check/proof/source edges; missing-check and unjustified-elision rejection. For SAFE1/SAFE2/SAFE8/SAFE9/SAFE15, invalidate or regenerate affected facts after source, expansion, type/effect, profile/target, numeric mode, memory/capability provider, pass/backend, dependency, grant or replay changes. Verify imported certificate schema, exact inputs, compatibility and trust before use. Erase only the exact proved condition with surviving backend assumptions and recorded check/proof identities; restore the check or reject on invalidation. Manual review alone is insufficient unless governing claim policy explicitly permits it; authority, audit, replay and human-review gates retain their separate policy obligations. Criterion `runtime/check-proof-preservation`: Retain required bounds/numeric/initialization/alias/resource checks or applicable proof/trap/rejection evidence, including source/check identity and elision provenance. Accepted fixture: Preserve source/check identity and valid bounds/numeric/initialization/alias/resource proofs across lowering and runtime/target service boundaries. Negative fixture: On invalidation regenerate proof, retain the required check/trap or reject; reject proofless elision or lost policy evidence. Required evidence: check/proof/elision provenance and invalidation/rejection fixtures; bind source/compiler/profile/target/provider identities, source-mapped stable diagnostics and every applicable source facet field/exception/negative condition listed for this criterion in specs/requirement-reconciliation/domain-gap-completion.edn. Dependencies consume mir/current-evidence-and-remaining-work/mir2-attach-fact-tables, lower/current-evidence-and-remaining-work/lower4-preserve-proofs-and-origins outputs under their stated contracts; no whole-component completion prerequisite. Status: Open; implementation acceptance unassessed."},
