     "- [ ] `lower/current-evidence-and-remaining-work/lower1-validate-lowering-inputs` lower/1: Validate lowering inputs\n\nCurrent evidence/status: Open; partial source evidence above is not closure\n\nDone when (yes/no): Reject unverified/stale IR and incompatible profiles/features; expose explicit supported-operation and target matrices. P5: admit SIMD/intrinsics only with declared target features, numeric mode and alignment/layout evidence plus a valid fallback or rejection. A target wrapper does not justify unchecked intrinsics or change source legality; guarded variant selection and target lowering remain distinct interfaces. Foundation requirement gravity/multiversion-guard-manifest: For every dispatched backend variant emit target-feature guards, profile and numeric/safety constraints, fallback/rejection behavior and source-bound benchmark evidence; exercise each variant and guard failure. Refusals: Reject an unguarded unavailable instruction, widened profile, unjustified fast path, absent valid fallback or a benchmark from a different variant/target. Evidence: retain the exact source/compiler/profile/target and applicable provider/checker identities, actual positive products and negative diagnostics for this criterion. Consume these actual dependency artifacts (not whole-component completion): legality/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/complete-profile-restrictions-and-generated-form-checks - Expanded source profile/effect/grant facts and checked/delegated/rejected legality products; pass-evidence - Actual subject-bound checker/proof/certificate/audit/replay/test evidence and verdicts. Foundation requirement gravity/target-lowering-operation-contract: For every MIR/domain operation in the declared input closure emit its explicit accept/lower/delegate/reject disposition with target, profile, ABI/provider and preservation obligations, and consume that disposition at target emission. Refusals: Reject an uncovered operation, stale/unverified IR, unsupported feature or delegate that widens effects/authority or drops source/safety/proof facts; emit an owning unsupported-operation diagnostic. Evidence: retain the exact source/compiler/profile/target and applicable provider/checker identities, actual positive products and negative diagnostics for this criterion. Consume these actual dependency artifacts (not whole-component completion): pipeline - Versioned stage contracts and actual compiler stage/fact/origin products; runtime/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/implement-explicit-family-selection-and-no-runtime-rejection - Selected runtime/provider service contracts and actual link/load/service-use evidence; legality/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/complete-profile-restrictions-and-generated-form-checks - Expanded source profile/effect/grant facts and checked/delegated/rejected legality products. Criterion profile-gap/native/feature-guard (Open): Input: Native SIMD/intrinsic lowering or shipped variant with declared feature, numeric semantics, alignment/layout, portable wrapper or target namespace and fallback/rejection policy. Accept: Check feature-specific lowering eligibility and separately select a shipped variant only under guards matching target/numeric/layout assumptions; retain a valid fallback or explicit rejection. Unchecked intrinsics remain unsafe. Reject: Missing/unavailable target feature, implicit backend numeric behavior, unsupported alignment/layout, invalid guarded variant/fallback or unchecked intrinsic presented as safe. Required outputs: SIMD/target feature and numeric/layout/guard report, eligible/ineligible target and fallback fixtures, P5-SIMD/NUMERIC or lowering diagnostic with feature/provider/proof/origin context. Dependencies: backend-interface, opt/current-evidence-and-remaining-work/opt2-implement-structural-families, legality/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/complete-profile-restrictions-and-generated-form-checks interface facts, not whole-task completion. Exact source predicates and frozen evidence: specs/requirement-reconciliation/profile-system/gap-completion.edn, mapping native/feature-guard; all attached contextual and negative predicates remain required. No implementation acceptance is inferred."},
