     "- [ ] `firmware` Firmware / `firmware`\n\nStatus: Open\n\nDeclared completion and remaining work: Adopt device memory/startup target; implement interrupt/MMIO/startup and explicit allocation; verify image/link map and rejected unsupported services on execution or named emulator. DOM2 acceptance requires memory map, startup/reset, interrupt vectors, stack/static-allocation/section and panic/BSP records; typed volatile/ordered/capability-checked MMIO and audited wrappers; declared interrupt effects and synchronization. Exercise timer sensor reset/acknowledgement/buffer/panic behavior and UART, reject hidden hosted services and unauthorized MMIO, and emit image/link/source/audit maps with boot/simulator evidence. Dependencies: profile legality, native lowering and runtime memory/startup boundaries; physical memory representability remains separate from removed project accounting ; P6 target conformance requires explicit stack/static/region/arena/provider capacity/reset/failure policy and no hidden GC/host services; unknown stack use rejects in strict mode. Check device-map address/width/alignment/volatility/order/grants, interrupt source/priority/shared-state/atomic/reentrancy/stack/latency/context, and required physical loop/recursion/blocking-timeout evidence; missing evidence rejects or requires the policy-permitted unsafe audit. Reject invalid maps, missing device authority, host calls and unbounded handler behavior. Emit image/linker/memory/device/vector/interrupt/latency/safety manifests with source provenance. Physical memory/timing requirements are not compiler work allowances; product target choice remains unassessed Foundation requirement gravity/realtime-not-throughput-proof: For a realtime claim record the declared deadline and worst-case execution/latency/jitter assumptions, target, interference, allocation/blocking/interrupt policy and applicable analysis or measurement evidence; retain throughput benchmarks as a different evidence class. Refusals: Reject deadline guarantees inferred from mean throughput, a different target/load, missing worst-case assumptions or hidden blocking/allocation; physical timing constraints are not compiler work quotas. Evidence: retain the exact source/compiler/profile/target and applicable provider/checker identities, actual positive products and negative diagnostics for this criterion. Consume these actual dependency artifacts (not whole-component completion): runtime/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/implement-explicit-family-selection-and-no-runtime-rejection - Selected runtime/provider service contracts and actual link/load/service-use evidence; pass-evidence - Actual subject-bound checker/proof/certificate/audit/replay/test evidence and verdicts.. Criterion profile-gap/firmware/device-mmio (Open): Input: Firmware source device operation and device map with base/register offsets, access direction, width, alignment, volatility, order and hardware capability. Accept: Admit typed MMIO only when the map, address/width/alignment/access, volatile/ordering rules and scope agree; require the declared typed wrapper or reviewed unsafe island for raw device operations. Reject: Absent or inconsistent device map, invalid address/width/alignment/access/order, missing device authority and raw address arithmetic presented as ordinary safe MMIO. Required outputs: MMIO/device map, wrapper/audit evidence and accepted/invalid-map/missing-grant diagnostics carrying target/device/region/span/generated-origin/effect/capability and missing proof. Dependencies: devices, legality/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/complete-profile-restrictions-and-generated-form-checks, auth/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/enforce-grant-intersection-attenuation-revocation-phase-and-lifetime interface facts, not whole-task completion. Exact source predicates and frozen evidence: specs/requirement-reconciliation/profile-system/gap-completion.edn, mapping firmware/device-mmio; all attached contextual and negative predicates remain required. No implementation acceptance is inferred. Criterion profile-gap/firmware/interrupt-contract (Open): Input: Firmware interrupt handler with source/vector, priority, latency and stack requirements, capabilities, shared state, atomic/critical-section and reentrancy context. Accept: Validate handler authority, target context, stack/latency and shared-state safety; preserve declared priority, reentrancy and synchronization; permit only the declared bounded provider/context behavior. Reject: Unbounded allocation or indefinite blocking, host services, invalid captures, missing interrupt authority, invalid shared-state/atomic discipline or unsatisfied required stack/latency evidence. Required outputs: Interrupt capability/vector table, stack/latency/shared-state report, handler acceptance/rejection fixtures and P6-INTERRUPT/P6-CAPABILITY or relevant proof diagnostic with origin/context. Dependencies: devices, legality/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/complete-profile-restrictions-and-generated-form-checks, auth/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/enforce-grant-intersection-attenuation-revocation-phase-and-lifetime interface facts, not whole-task completion. Exact source predicates and frozen evidence: specs/requirement-reconciliation/profile-system/gap-completion.edn, mapping firmware/interrupt-contract; all attached contextual and negative predicates remain required. No implementation acceptance is inferred. Criterion profile-gap/firmware/physical-timing-contract (Open): Input: Firmware call graph and realtime-affecting loops, recursion, stack, interrupts, blocking and allocation under explicit physical target policy. Accept: Check required loop/recursion/worst-case stack/interrupt-latency/blocking-timeout/allocation evidence against actual declared physical constraints; unknown stack rejects in strict mode; missing evidence rejects or follows only the explicitly permitted unsafe-audit policy. Reject: Missing/exceeded physical evidence, indefinite blocking and hidden runtime assumptions; never substitute compiler work counters or fabricated project allowances for physical timing proof. Required outputs: Loop/latency/stack/allocation constraint and proof report with target/span/generated-origin/device/interrupt/required-bound information and accepted/rejected/conditional-audit cases. Dependencies: legality/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/complete-profile-restrictions-and-generated-form-checks, lower/current-evidence-and-remaining-work/lower1-validate-lowering-inputs interface facts, not whole-task completion. Exact source predicates and frozen evidence: specs/requirement-reconciliation/profile-system/gap-completion.edn, mapping firmware/physical-timing-contract; all attached contextual and negative predicates remain required. No implementation acceptance is inferred. Criterion profile-gap/firmware/profile-memory-contract (Open): Input: Firmware namespace/call graph and stack/static/region/arena or explicitly permitted bounded provider, image/linker/memory/vector/device contracts. Accept: Check visible memory regime, stack/static physical representation and provider capacity/reset/failure behavior; emit the firmware image layout with linker, memory map, vector and device identity plus safety/provenance evidence. A specifically introduced bounded runtime exception must remain explicit. Reject: Hidden or unbounded allocation, undeclared GC/host services, unknown stack in strict mode, unsupported unwinding/dynamic loading and runtime AI/tool calls. Required outputs: Firmware profile/image/linker/memory/device/vector manifests, stack/static and bounded-allocation reports, no-hidden-runtime acceptance and GC/host/allocation/stack/static rejection diagnostics. Dependencies: legality/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/complete-profile-restrictions-and-generated-form-checks, lower/current-evidence-and-remaining-work/lower1-validate-lowering-inputs, runtime/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/implement-memory-concurrency-and-typed-ffi-boundaries interface facts, not whole-task completion. Exact source predicates and frozen evidence: specs/requirement-reconciliation/profile-system/gap-completion.edn, mapping firmware/profile-memory-contract; all attached contextual and negative predicates remain required. No implementation acceptance is inferred. For this target, the architecture owner records the concrete target/ABI, accepted artifact kind, named simulator/device evidence and required service set before implementation scope is claimed. Reject a scope claim missing any required selection or incompatible with the declared profile; no target or product is selected by this task. Target integration consumes the exact Lower/Emit artifact and explicit runtime or no-runtime manifest plus required standard-library adapters. Record actual simulation/execution and applicable layout, clock, interrupt, unsafe-island, grant and source-to-artifact provenance checks; reject forbidden services, missing adapters, unauditable authority or a record-only execution claim. These target gates do not require completion of the full Platform Product.. Criterion `domain/firmware-image-production`: Produce target-specific firmware images with explicit startup/memory/section/BSP boundaries, source/audit/link maps and required boot evidence. Accepted fixture: Emit firmware with target memory map, startup/reset, vectors, stack/static allocation/sections, panic and BSP boundaries. Negative fixture: Reject incomplete startup/layout, unsupported hosted services, unaudited MMIO or absent boot evidence. Required evidence: firmware image, source/link/audit maps and boot/simulator report; bind source/compiler/profile/target/provider identities, source-mapped stable diagnostics and every applicable source facet field/exception/negative condition listed for this criterion in specs/requirement-reconciliation/domain-gap-completion.edn. Dependencies consume backend-c, runtime/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/implement-explicit-family-selection-and-no-runtime-rejection outputs under their stated contracts; no whole-component completion prerequisite. Status: Open; implementation acceptance unassessed. Criterion `domain/firmware-sensor-integration`: Execute the declared timer-driven sensor firmware slice and reject forbidden MMIO/interrupt/runtime use. Accepted fixture: Run timer-driven sensor reset, interrupt acknowledgement, ADC schema, static buffer writes and panic behavior on a named substrate. Negative fixture: Reject forbidden MMIO/interrupt/runtime use and undeclared effects or allocation policy. Required evidence: sensor firmware image, vector/link records and simulator trace; bind source/compiler/profile/target/provider identities, source-mapped stable diagnostics and every applicable source facet field/exception/negative condition listed for this criterion in specs/requirement-reconciliation/domain-gap-completion.edn. Dependencies consume backend-c, runtime/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/implement-explicit-family-selection-and-no-runtime-rejection outputs under their stated contracts; no whole-component completion prerequisite. Status: Open; implementation acceptance unassessed.\n\nSource basis: [Firmware contract](../../docs/phase-09-domain-specific-computing-coverage/125-dom2-firmware-and-embedded-domain-specification.md)"},
