rtifact kind, named simulator/device evidence and required service set before implementation scope is claimed. Reject a scope claim missing any required selection or incompatible with the declared profile; no target or product is selected by this task. Target integration consumes the exact Lower/Emit artifact and explicit runtime or no-runtime manifest plus required standard-library adapters. Record actual simulation/execution and applicable layout, clock, interrupt, unsafe-island, grant and source-to-artifact provenance checks; reject forbidden services, missing adapters, unauditable authority or a record-only execution claim. These target gates do not require completion of the full Platform Product.. Criterion `domain/kernel-artifact-production`: Produce source-linked kernel artifact, unsafe audit/capability manifests and emulator smoke evidence for the declared kernel slice. Accepted fixture: Emit the declared kernel object/boot image with syscall/interrupt tables, ABI, unsafe-audit, capability and source/debug maps. Negative fixture: Reject missing audit/provenance or claims lacking named emulator smoke evidence. Required evidence: kernel artifact pack and emulator smoke report; bind source/compiler/profile/target/provider identities, source-mapped stable diagnostics and every applicable source facet field/exception/negative condition listed for this criterion in specs/requirement-reconciliation/domain-gap-completion.edn. Dependencies consume backend-llvm, legality/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/complete-ownership-borrow-initialization-and-lifetime-analysis outputs under their stated contracts; no whole-component completion prerequisite. Status: Open; implementation acceptance unassessed. Criterion `domain/kernel-syscall-integration`: Execute the declared typed syscall on the named emulator/substrate with accepted/rejected authority and memory-boundary cases. Accepted fixture: Invoke the typed syscall on the named emulator/substrate with user-pointer taint, raw wrapper/bounds, authority, context and error mapping. Negative fixture: Reject unauthorized or invalid user-memory input and hosted runtime assumptions. Required evidence: syscall table, valid/invalid invocation trace and denial diagnostics; bind source/compiler/profile/target/provider identities, source-mapped stable diagnostics and every applicable source facet field/exception/negative condition listed for this criterion in specs/requirement-reconciliation/domain-gap-completion.edn. Dependencies consume backend-llvm, legality/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/complete-ownership-borrow-initialization-and-lifetime-analysis outputs under their stated contracts; no whole-component completion prerequisite. Status: Open; implementation acceptance unassessed. Criterion `domain/kernel-user-boundary`: Enforce typed syscall/user-kernel input, taint, capability and error contracts with audited privileged implementation boundaries. Accepted fixture: Enforce declared syscall schemas, user-pointer validation/taint, capabilities and error translation through audited privileged wrappers. Negative fixture: Reject schema-less/taint-unsafe entry, unaudited raw memory and ambient authority. Required evidence: kernel ABI/syscall schema, wrapper audit and boundary fixtures; bind source/compiler/profile/target/provider identities, source-mapped stable diagnostics and every applicable source facet field/exception/negative condition listed for this criterion in specs/requirement-reconciliation/domain-gap-completion.edn. Dependencies consume backend-llvm, legality/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/complete-ownership-borrow-initialization-and-lifetime-analysis outputs under their stated contracts; no whole-component completion prerequisite. Status: Open; implementation acceptance unassessed.\n\nSource basis: [Kernel contract](../../docs/phase-09-domain-specific-computing-coverage/126-dom3-operating-system-and-kernel-domain-specification.md)"},
