     "- [ ] `release/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/build-reproducible-signed-distributions-with-provenancesbom` Build reproducible signed distributions with provenance/SBOM\n\nStatus: Open\n\nEvidence baseline: [Artifact provenance](../../docs/phase-15-bootstrap-and-self-hosting/210-boot8-bootstrap-artifact-provenance-specification.md)\n\nClosing evidence: Rebuild identity and signature/provenance verification plus tamper rejection BOOT1/BOOT6/BOOT8: Retain locked dependencies, recipe and environment controls for time/locale/filesystem order/toolchain/network, compiler lineage and manifest/content-hash comparisons. Declare unsupported rebuild strategies; diverse rebuilds require independent toolchain identity. Reproducibility exceptions and accepted deltas require recorded review. Produce canonical signed provenance binding stage/artifact/source graph/compiler/lockfile/recipe/environment/dependencies/builder and conformance/equivalence/safety/SBOM/signature links. Auditor queries must traverse release compiler to seed inputs; permit only explicitly declared stage cycles. Reject lineage gaps, undeclared cycles, uncontrolled network inputs, noncanonical signing, missing required evidence, unexplained drift and revoked compiler/builder/dependency/signature inputs. Release extension release/final-rebuild-reproducibility: Rebuild the actual final gravity artifact at least twice from the recorded recipe, locked inputs and environment. Compare binary, provenance, SBOM, signing-record and command-contract evidence identities; retain both actual rebuild outputs and comparison report. Reject missing rebuilds/comparisons, unexplained drift and supplied-record substitution. Earlier hosted packaging reproducibility cannot close final release rebuilds. Release extension release/final-supply-chain-governance-bundle: Produce and validate the selected actual final release's provenance, SBOM, canonical signing records, release notes, target-support policy, compatibility, security-review and governance approval evidence. Bind records to actual binary, recipe/environment, source/compiler/dependency/target identities and accepted command evidence. Reject missing, stale, tampered, revoked or mismatched records, unsupported targets and governance gaps with applicable P18T06001-P18T06008 blockers. A hosted bundle is not final seedless evidence."},
