     "- [ ] `runtime/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/connect-distributedai-replay-and-interactive-execution` Connect distributed/AI replay and interactive execution\n\nStatus: Open\n\nEvidence baseline: [Runtime contracts](../../docs/phase-08-runtime-architecture/README.md)\n\nClosing evidence: Recorded nondeterminism, replay equality, no undeclared duplicated external effect, REPL grant denial. R6/R7/R8/R9: topology/provider/event-log/state/message schemas; durable idempotency, timeout/retry/cancellation/failure/compensation records; migration or rejection of replay-incompatible code/topology/schema changes; model/provider/prompt provenance, output and sink validation, policy-recorded provider substitution, typed tool contracts with caller/callee grants and policy-required human review, memory/retrieval privacy/retention/deletion/taint controls and secret redaction; R7/R8 replay-required segments return recorded model/tool/retrieval/memory/review decisions or reject a missing record. R6 concurrency fixtures accept an authorized graph-declared replay-safe repetition where no R7/R8 recorded-output obligation applies; the declaration never grants authority or overrides those recorded-output obligations. Interactive forms and generated code pass the ordinary compiler checks before execution; session manifests, transcripts, evaluated forms, syntax/core/MIR/source snapshots capture build-affecting state or mark nonhermeticity, and hot reload invalidates stale analysis/backend/runtime/package outputs. Reject undeclared repeated external calls, live nondeterministic calls in R7/R8 recorded-output segments even with a replay-safe graph declaration, repetitions without required authority, unvalidated trusted sinks, forbidden-profile eval, hidden interactive IO and stale reload artifacts. Dependencies: Domains supplies agent/workflow contracts, Schema supplies validators/migrations, Build consumes session inputs and invalidation, Auth supplies grants and review policy. Project work/token/call/time/retry allowances are removed admission requirements; actual provider billing/account limits remain external, and semantic failure/cancellation policy remains required. R8 mixed budget spans retain unresolved qualification in the family proposal.. Under [SAFE8/SAFE13](../../docs/phase-02-safety/README.md), retain signal/timer/retry/idempotency/compensation and tool failure records; exact replay consumes recorded model/tool outputs, while audit policy retains digests, schemas, decisions, review events and providers. None is allowed only in interactive or non-safe contexts; workflow and release claims require replay or audit. Execute retention/deletion and secret-tainted memory denial fixtures through the declared provider; prompt text never grants authority. Residual criterion runtime/hot-reload-invalidation: For a changed interactive definition, record changed source, affected namespace/dependency edges and invalidation of stale syntax, analysis, typed core, MIR/domain IR, backend, runtime and package artifacts. Emit a hot-reload/session record distinguishing preserved runtime state from state that must restart, with evaluated-form/source/generated-origin identity. Show an unaffected artifact retained and affected artifacts rebuilt or rejected before reuse; reject a stale analysis/MIR/backend/runtime/package artifact, untracked build-affecting state and debug inspection outside grants/secret policy. Build-affecting session inputs are captured or explicitly nonhermetic; interactive manifests do not imply release runtime support. Build-affecting sessions emit transcripts, evaluated-form artifacts, syntax/core/MIR snapshots, dependency invalidation records and source maps; debug hooks cannot expose raw memory, host process state or model/tool outputs without grants."},
