     "- [ ] `tools/finite-service-outcomes-and-remaining-work/profile-performance-tool-maintainer` Profile / performance-tool maintainer\n\nStatus: Open\n\nRemaining implementation tasks: Capture real supported target samples; bind environment and source/artifact identity; report overhead, comparisons and safety-check evidence\n\nClosing evidence and governing contract: Samples measured rather than generated? Unavailable counters explicit? No unrelated grant or proofless elision? [Profiler](../../docs/phase-13-tooling-and-developer-experience/187-t11-profiler-and-performance-inspector-design.md) Verify benchmark/profile/target/artifact/environment/compiler and applicable device identity, source/MIR/sample links, measured or explicitly unknown overhead, structured trace/environment/comparison/regression/layout reports and policy thresholds. Separate model/tool latency, retry, replay and human-review time and actual external costs. Reject incompatible benchmark comparison unless policy permits normalization, unsupported counters, exceeded regression thresholds, missing check-elision evidence and unrelated grants. PERF5/D6/TEST12 benchmark producer: emit a machine-readable benchmark manifest with workload/dataset/seed, profile/target/artifact/source/compiler/backend/runtime/provider/dependency versions, input/layout, metric/units, warmup, samples, statistical method, variance/repeat policy, correctness/safety gates, threshold and harness. Capture hardware/features/OS/kernel/build/power/thermal fingerprint and counter source/support, raw samples, summary, baseline and attributable comparison/replay inputs. Cover core/numeric/dispatch/layout/FFI/concurrency/IO/GPU/workflow/compiler/build families; AI reports separately show model, tool, memory, human-review and replay latency/cost, preserving external billing. Reproduce historical measurements from stored identities; accept only compatible fingerprints/artifacts or explicitly reviewed normalization. Gate performance only after actual correctness/safety/precision/profile/replay checks, with proof for check-elision gains. Reject missing identity/metadata, unsupported counters, opaque AI totals, single-sample release gates and correctness-masking wins; emit PERF5/TEST12 structured diagnostics and accepted/rejected benchmark fixtures. PERF5/TEST12 baseline governance: deterministically classify no-regression, noise, environment drift, compiler/backend/runtime/provider/dependency regression, semantic/safety change and invalid baseline using explicit thresholds and variance/repeat policy. Fail threshold-exceeding comparisons unless accepted drift/intentional semantic policy applies; compare different artifacts or fingerprints only with approved normalization. Version the baseline registry and preserve benchmark/source/package/compiler/backend/environment/sample/threshold/review-owner/date history plus reviewed update record. Never hide correctness/safety failures by replacing a baseline. Exercise accepted reviewed updates and rejected unreviewed/stale baselines, noise, drift, incompatible normalization, threshold breaches and failed gates; emit regression decision, baseline diff/history and PERF5/TEST12 diagnostics containing benchmark/profile/target/metric/baseline/fingerprint/summary/threshold/gate state. PERF6 production-trace privacy: capture PGO summaries only under explicit access/retention/data policy; redact or aggregate tainted/secret-derived values, with governed raw-data handling only where policy permits. Emit privacy/redaction/aggregation/retention/access records linked to profile-data and public build artifact identities. Exercise actual capture/export consumers with user inputs, credentials/secrets, prompts, tool outputs and customer data; verify forbidden raw values never enter public artifacts, required redaction survives transformation and retention/access denials prevent the operation. Report violations as PERF6 privacy diagnostics with data/policy/workload/pass/profile/target and offending field; schema presence alone is insufficient."},
